(
  'Misinformation Kills: The Real-World Cost of Fake News and Why Verification Matters',
  'misinformation-kills-real-world-cost-fake-news',
  E'## This Isn''t Just About "Fake News"\n\nLet''s stop treating misinformation as an internet nuisance. **People are dying.**\n\nIn 2020, an Iranian news outlet reported that drinking methanol could cure COVID-19. Over **700 people died** and 5,000 were hospitalized after following this false claim. In India, WhatsApp rumors about child kidnappers led to **33 mob killings** of innocent people in a single year.\n\nMisinformation isn''t a social media problem. It''s a **public health crisis, a national security threat, and a human rights emergency.**\n\n### The Global Cost\n\n| Impact Area | Annual Cost/Impact |\n|---|---|\n| Global economy | $78 billion in damages |\n| Healthcare | 30% of patients received wrong treatment based on false health info |\n| Democracy | 87 countries experienced organized disinformation campaigns |\n| Social cohesion | 64% of people say fake news has damaged their trust in institutions |\n| Mental health | Exposure to health misinformation increases anxiety by 40% |\n\n### The Speed Problem\n\nMIT research proves that **false news spreads 6x faster** than truth on social media. By the time a fact-check is published:\n\n- The false claim has been seen by **millions**\n- It has been shared across **multiple platforms**\n- People have already **acted on it**\n- The emotional damage is **already done**\n\nThis is why reactive fact-checking isn''t enough. We need **proactive verification infrastructure.**\n\n### Who Profits from Lies?\n\nMisinformation isn''t random — it''s an industry:\n\n- **Click farms** generate $300M+ annually from fake news engagement\n- **Foreign state actors** spend billions on disinformation operations\n- **Scammers** use false health/financial claims to steal from vulnerable people\n- **Political operatives** weaponize misinformation to swing elections\n\n### Why Traditional Fact-Checking Fails\n\n1. **Too slow** — Takes days, damage done in hours\n2. **Too centralized** — A few newsrooms can''t cover everything\n3. **Limited reach** — Fact-checks rarely reach the people who saw the original lie\n4. **No incentive** — Nobody gets rewarded for finding the truth\n\n### The TrustLighthouse Solution\n\nWe''re building the **opposite** of everything that makes misinformation win:\n\n- ⚡ **Fast** — AI-assisted verification in minutes, not days\n- 🌐 **Decentralized** — Thousands of verifiers across the globe\n- 💰 **Incentivized** — Bounties and rewards for accurate verification\n- 📱 **Accessible** — Works on any smartphone, anywhere\n- 🔗 **Permanent** — Verifications recorded on blockchain via NFT badges\n\n### What You Can Do Right Now\n\nYou don''t need to be a journalist or an expert. You just need to care about truth.\n\n1. **Start verifying** — Every claim you check helps\n2. **Earn while you learn** — Bounties reward your time\n3. **Share verified information** — Become a truth amplifier\n4. **Report misinformation** — Flag false claims for the community\n5. **Join a Lighthouse Room** — Collaborate with other truth-seekers\n\n> "The only thing necessary for misinformation to triumph is for truth-seekers to do nothing."\n\n**The cost of inaction is measured in lives. The cost of action? A few minutes of your day.**\n\nStart verifying on TrustLighthouse today.',
  'Misinformation kills. 700+ died from false COVID cures. $78B in global damages annually. Learn why verification is a life-or-death matter and how you can help.',
  '/blog/misinformation-kills-cover.jpg',
