(
  'Why You Can''t Trust What You See on Social Media (And What To Do About It)',
  'cant-trust-social-media-what-to-do',
  E'## Your Feed is Lying to You\n\nYou scroll through Twitter. A shocking statistic catches your eye. You share it. Your followers share it. Within hours, thousands of people believe something that was **completely fabricated.**\n\nThis happens **millions of times every day.**\n\n### The Algorithm Problem\n\nSocial media algorithms don''t optimize for truth. They optimize for **engagement.** And nothing engages like outrage, fear, and shock.\n\n**The math is brutal:**\n- False claims get **70% more retweets** than accurate ones\n- Emotionally charged misinformation gets **3x more comments**\n- Algorithms boost content that keeps you scrolling — not content that''s true\n\nYou''re not dumb for falling for it. **The system is designed to fool you.**\n\n### The Deepfake Revolution\n\nIt''s about to get much worse.\n\n- AI can now generate **photo-realistic fake images** in seconds\n- **Voice cloning** can make anyone say anything\n- **Video deepfakes** are becoming indistinguishable from reality\n- By 2026, experts predict **90% of online content** will be AI-generated\n\nIf you can''t trust your eyes and ears, what can you trust?\n\n### The 5-Second Verification Habit\n\nBefore you share anything, take 5 seconds:\n\n1. **Source check** — Who published this? Do they have a track record?\n2. **Date check** — Is this current or recycled old news?\n3. **Emotion check** — Is this designed to make you angry/scared? That''s a red flag.\n4. **Cross-reference** — Can you find this from a second reputable source?\n5. **Verify on TrustLighthouse** — Paste the claim and get AI-powered analysis\n\n### Building Your Personal Trust Filter\n\nTrustLighthouse gives you tools to become misinformation-proof:\n\n- 🔍 **Instant claim verification** — Paste any claim, get analysis in minutes\n- 📊 **Source credibility scores** — Know which sources to trust at a glance\n- 🔔 **Viral claim alerts** — Get notified when trending claims are debunked\n- 🧠 **Media literacy training** — Level up your critical thinking skills\n- 🏅 **Earn while you verify** — Turn your skepticism into income\n\n### The Social Media Detox You Actually Need\n\nYou don''t need to quit social media. You need to **upgrade how you use it.**\n\nInstead of passively consuming, become an active verifier:\n- Check before you share\n- Call out misinformation politely with verified sources\n- Follow fact-checking accounts and communities\n- Earn bounties by verifying claims others are sharing\n\n### The Ripple Effect\n\nEvery time you verify instead of blindly sharing:\n- You protect your **reputation**\n- You protect your **followers**\n- You make social media **slightly more truthful**\n- You earn **trust capital** that compounds over time\n\n> "In a world of infinite content and zero trust, the person who verifies before sharing isn''t paranoid — they''re powerful."\n\n**Stop being part of the problem. Start being the solution.**',
  'Social media algorithms optimize for engagement, not truth. False claims get 70% more retweets. Learn the 5-second verification habit that protects you and your followers.',
  '/blog/social-media-trust-cover.jpg',
  'media-literacy',
